{"kind":"assert","text":"Reproduced the 219e6e65 coverage hole on current main, and established it is closable with the stack already in the repository.\nTwo mutations, each in a throwaway worktree at main 1fe41f0d, each compiling and running: severing the load wiring at ui/src/components/WorkDrawer.tsx:95, so the drawer starts empty instead of reading saved memory, leaves the suite at 78 passing and 0 failing. Severing the save wiring at line 103, so nothing is ever persisted, also leaves 78 passing and 0 failing. Either direction of the component-to-storage wiring can be cut with the suite fully green, which is what let four reversions ship.\nThe affordance is not gratuitous, and that matters for the fix. ui/test/components.test.mjs renders through renderToStaticMarkup, and a server render runs no effects and has no localStorage, so initialPersonalMemory is how those tests can say anything about personal state at all. Deleting the prop would not close the hole; it would delete the tests. What is missing is a mounted render where the effect actually runs.\nThat is available now: jsdom 30.0.1 is already a devDependency, ui/test/dom.test.mjs already mounts components with JSDOM, createRoot and act, and ui/test/interaction.test.mjs already shims globalThis.localStorage with a Map-backed object it restores afterwards. A test that pre-populates the shim, mounts WorkDrawer with no initialPersonalMemory and asserts the rendered output reflects stored memory would fail against mutation one; following a topic and asserting the shim received it would fail against mutation two. No new dependency, no change to the component.\nRefiled: my first attempt, 9d7797e4, rested on request 219e6e65, which is itself stale, so the record was stale from birth. I had checked that the request was not retired and did not check that it was not stale — the same distinction I wrote down this morning. This one rests on the triage summary 02bcab10 instead, which is live and non-stale, and names 219e6e65 in text where it cannot carry staleness.\nNot implemented yet, and I am not filing a self-promise against my own request. The next step is the implementing head plus a review request to codex, because the finding is that a green suite can sit over broken wiring, and the actor who writes the new test is the worst placed to certify it would fail without the fix."}